<task id="060" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Repoint 4 server-side C# deep-links → openSpaarkeAi shape</title>
    <phase>6 Retirement</phase>
    <gate>blocked — 052 (openSpaarkeAi param extension must exist)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies compiled C# in Sprk.Bff.Api (bff tag); the current deep-links would 404 post-retirement, so correctness is load-bearing; test update required (HandoffUrlBuilderTests).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Bounded repoint of a known URL shape across 4 call-sites with a reference target (openSpaarkeAi); no architectural judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Ordered retirement head (§13.5): this repoint MUST land before any delete task (063) so no deep-link dangles; sequenced after 052.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>052</deps>
    <tags>bff, retirement</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Repoint the four server-side C# deep-links that currently target the retiring sprk_analysisworkspace code page so
    they instead build the openSpaarkeAi `sprk_spaarkeai` deep-link shape (the target extended in task 052). These are
    compiled URLs that would 404 the moment the web resource is deleted (063); repointing first is the ordered §13.5
    invariant. Update HandoffUrlBuilderTests to assert the new shape.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the BFF agent/analysis handoff surface and the openSpaarkeAi deep-link
    contract. Follow ADRs strictly; do NOT fork Services/Ai (redesign-r2 sole owner) — this task only touches URL-builder
    and notification actionUrl code.
  </role>

  <goal>
    HandoffUrlBuilder.BuildAnalysisWorkspaceUrl and its three callers plus the AnalysisEndpoints notification actionUrl
    all emit the openSpaarkeAi `sprk_spaarkeai` deep-link; HandoffUrlBuilderTests assert the new shape; a Grep for
    `sprk_analysisworkspace` across C# returns zero; BFF build is green.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec §13.5 / FR-18, the sprk_analysisworkspace code page is being retired. Four compiled C# deep-links point at
      it and would 404 after deletion: HandoffUrlBuilder.BuildAnalysisWorkspaceUrl (the builder) and its three callers
      (PlaybookStatusEndpoints, PlaybookInvocationService, AgentErrorHandler), plus the notification actionUrl in
      AnalysisEndpoints (webresourceName=sprk_analysisworkspace). Task 052 already extended openSpaarkeAi to carry
      analysisId/worktype/regarding on the `sprk_spaarkeai` surface — that is the repoint target. This is the first of the
      ordered retirement tasks: repoint before delete.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/HandoffUrlBuilder.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/PlaybookStatusEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/PlaybookInvocationService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/AgentErrorHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/Agent/HandoffUrlBuilderTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/utils/launch-resolver.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="052" status="pending">Extends openSpaarkeAi with analysisId/worktype/regarding on the sprk_spaarkeai surface — the repoint target shape.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: only HandoffUrlBuilder + its 3 callers + AnalysisEndpoints.cs:783 notification actionUrl are repointed. Do NOT touch Services/Ai orchestration internals (redesign-r2 sole owner) beyond swapping the URL string these builders emit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">SCOPE: the repointed deep-link resolves to the sprk_spaarkeai surface via the openSpaarkeAi shape (record-driven opens stay in code); do NOT route through surfaceLaunchRegistry.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">SCOPE: this is a BFF-touching task — run the publish-size check and report absolute size + diff vs the ~49.63 MB baseline in task notes / PR (CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). A string-only repoint is expected to be size-neutral.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: ordered §13.5 — this repoint MUST be complete before task 063 deletes the web resource; do NOT delete anything in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">SCOPE: if a caller needs AI capability it goes through Services/Ai/PublicContracts/; do NOT inject AI-internal types into the agent/notification code being edited.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/ASSISTANT-SURFACE-LAUNCH-MECHANISM.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="openSpaarkeAi deep-link shape" location="src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/utils/launch-resolver.ts">
        Read the openSpaarkeAi/openSpaarkeAiCompose resolver (~lines 198,268) to mirror the exact sprk_spaarkeai query-param shape the server URL must produce (analysisId/worktype/regarding).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare FULL rigor + reason; confirm task 052's openSpaarkeAi extension is merged so the target shape exists.</step>
    <step order="1">Read launch-resolver.ts openSpaarkeAi/openSpaarkeAiCompose to capture the exact sprk_spaarkeai deep-link shape (surface + query params analysisId/worktype/regarding).</step>
    <step order="2">Rewrite HandoffUrlBuilder.BuildAnalysisWorkspaceUrl (lines ~20-39) to emit the sprk_spaarkeai openSpaarkeAi shape instead of sprk_AnalysisWorkspaceLauncher; keep the method's inputs/signature stable unless the new shape requires added params.</step>
    <step order="3">Update the 3 callers to pass whatever the new shape needs: PlaybookStatusEndpoints.cs (~119-122), PlaybookInvocationService.cs (~268-274), AgentErrorHandler.cs (~102-110).</step>
    <step order="4">Repoint the notification actionUrl in AnalysisEndpoints.cs (~782-784): change webresourceName=sprk_analysisworkspace to the sprk_spaarkeai openSpaarkeAi shape.</step>
    <step order="5">Update HandoffUrlBuilderTests.cs to assert the new sprk_spaarkeai shape and remove any assertion on the old sprk_analysisworkspace URL.</step>
    <step order="6">Build the BFF (dotnet build) and run the affected tests; Grep the C# tree for `sprk_analysisworkspace` / `sprk_AnalysisWorkspaceLauncher` and confirm zero remaining references from this task's scope.</step>
    <step order="7">Run the publish-size check; record absolute size + diff in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 060 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the openSpaarkeAi shape from task 052 cannot represent a deep-link a caller needs (e.g. a notification actionUrl requires a param the client resolver does not parse), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than inventing a new URL contract.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build the BFF and run HandoffUrlBuilderTests.</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run the publish-size measurement and Grep verification.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/HandoffUrlBuilder.cs (+ 3 callers + AnalysisEndpoints.cs notification actionUrl)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/Agent/HandoffUrlBuilderTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the retirement is complete, when any of the 4 deep-links is built, then it resolves to the sprk_spaarkeai SpaarkeAi surface via the openSpaarkeAi shape (not a sprk_analysisworkspace / sprk_AnalysisWorkspaceLauncher URL).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">HandoffUrlBuilderTests assert the new sprk_spaarkeai shape and pass; the BFF build is green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep-clean: `sprk_analysisworkspace` and `sprk_AnalysisWorkspaceLauncher` return zero matches across the C# tree (excluding files deleted by later tasks).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no caller silently drops the analysisId/regarding context — a deep-link built for an existing analysis carries analysisId in the sprk_spaarkeai shape.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size reported (absolute + diff vs ~49.63 MB baseline); no new HIGH-severity CVE; size delta within NFR-01 thresholds.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec §13.5 / FR-18. Ordered head of the retirement chain: repoint before delete. Do NOT delete the web resource here
    (that is task 063). The sprk_spaarkeai target shape is defined by task 052's openSpaarkeAi extension.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
